WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.500
Week eleven.

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:03.006
Inside a media agency,

00:00:03.056 --> 00:00:07.200
with Ali Coysh from Initiative and Geoff Clarke from IPG Mediabrands.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.540
Media used to mean planning and buying paid space.

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:16.184
Now it orchestrates whole customer experiences, across owned, earned, shared and paid.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.172
Ali's logic flow runs from the journey stage,

00:00:19.222 --> 00:00:20.355
to the bond or barrier,

00:00:20.405 --> 00:00:21.270
to media role,

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:22.120
channel,

00:00:21.912 --> 00:00:22.712
platform,

00:00:22.648 --> 00:00:23.936
and environment.

00:00:24.533 --> 00:00:26.358
For NRMA in Queensland,

00:00:26.408 --> 00:00:29.405
that meant the highest non-customer consideration in six years,

00:00:29.455 --> 00:00:33.133
and a four hundred and sixty seven million dollar commitment to fix the Bruce Highway.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:38.170
Geoff's point: seventy percent of agency work is downstream, and still manual.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:39.531
Bots now handle setup,

00:00:39.581 --> 00:00:40.893
tracking and makegoods,

00:00:40.943 --> 00:00:43.317
saving two hundred and seven thousand hours.

00:00:43.933 --> 00:00:46.204
So the skills that matter are data driven thinking,

00:00:46.254 --> 00:00:47.054
creative and strategic thinking,

00:00:46.768 --> 00:00:48.939
and adaptability,

00:00:48.989 --> 00:00:50.541
with lifelong learning.

00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:52.210
The takeaway?

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.130
It's creative and media now.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:57.237
The lasting differentiator is the craft of your people.
